Spectral libraries
------------------
Location:  tetracorder/sl1/usgs/library06.conv/  (splib06b, sprlb06b)
             -- in the repository and in the container image. These are the
             unconvolved masters; the pipeline convolves them to each scene's
             wavelength grid at run time, so no convolved libraries are shipped.
Source:    Copied from spectroscopy-tetracorder (see above).
           splib06 is the USGS Digital Spectral Library:
           Clark, R.N., et al., 2007, USGS digital spectral library splib06a:
           U.S. Geological Survey, Digital Data Series 231,
           https://doi.org/10.3133/ds231
           sprlb06 is the companion research library distributed with
           Tetracorder.
License:   The library data are public domain. Upstream states this directly,
           in the license.txt carried in the library directory: "The USGS
           spectral library 06 is public domain data." The GPL-3.0 and PSI
           conditions described above attach to the software in those
           directories, not to the library data itself.

The library directory carries upstream's license.txt, reached as
AAAA.license.txt, restored from spectroscopy-tetracorder's
sl1/usgs/library06.conv/license.txt.


DaVinci
-------
Location:  vendor/davinci/src/  (vendored source, compiled into the container
           image; the source tree is itself carried in the image, see
           "Container images" below)
Upstream:  Arizona State University, Mars Space Flight Facility,
           https://davinci.asu.edu
Source:    https://oss.mars.asu.edu/svn/davinci/davinci/trunk
Revision:  r19810, version 3.02. vendor/davinci/refresh.sh reproduces the export.
Copyright: (c) Arizona State University and the DaVinci developers
           <davinci-dev@mars.asu.edu>.
License:   GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
           vendor/davinci/src/LICENSE is the GPL-2 text. The version-or-later
           grant is upstream's own, in vendor/davinci/src/contrib/debian/
           copyright, which applies "GPL-2+" to Files: *.

DaVinci is the language Tetracorder's colour products and browse images are
written in: the scripts under tetracorder/tetracorder.cmds/*/davinci-cmds.for.
usr.local.bin/ carry a "#!/usr/bin/env -S davinci -f" shebang and are
interpreted by it. They are data to DaVinci, not linked into it.

The image used to install ASU's prebuilt davinci_3.0.1-1_amd64_ubuntu22_04.deb.
Building from vendored source replaced that, which is what made an arm64 image
possible and what lets the corresponding source ship with the binary.

The tree under vendor/davinci/src/ is an unmodified export of upstream at
r19810. The build makes one change to it, in the Containerfile rather than in
the vendored tree, and only to build machinery: every config.guess and
config.sub (six of each, dated 2003-06-17 and predating aarch64) is replaced
with the current copy from Debian's autotools-dev (Copyright 1992-2022 Free
Software Foundation, Inc.). Those two files are GPL-3-or-later with the special
exception that covers their use in a configure script, are used only to run
configure, and are not installed into the image.

