Container images
----------------
A container image built from this repository is an aggregate of separate
programs. Each keeps its own license: tetrapy (Apache-2.0), Tetracorder and
specpr (GPL-3.0 with the PSI conditions), DaVinci (GPL-2.0-or-later), and the
Ubuntu, conda-forge and PyPI packages in the image (their own licenses). They
are combined as separate programs that run each other, not linked into a single
work, so no license here extends to another.

The complete corresponding source for the GPL components is inside the image,
not merely offered: the Containerfile's "COPY . ." puts the whole repository at
/root, so an image carries /root/vendor/davinci/src (DaVinci, GPL-2.0-or-later)
and /root/tetracorder (Tetracorder and specpr, GPL-3.0) as the source the
binaries in it were built from. This satisfies GPL-2 section 3(a) and GPL-3
section 6(a) directly, and no separate written offer is needed.

The same source is in this repository, at the commit the image was built from;
images published by .github/workflows/container.yml carry a build-provenance
attestation naming that commit.


